<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cerro del Villar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cerro del Villar is an archaeological site at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalhorce">Guadalhorce</a> river near Málaga in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, once an island in the river's estuary. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> founded a settlement there in the 8th century BCE, with houses, workshops and a busy harbour. It was largely abandoned in the 6th century BCE, when its people moved to Malaka, the future Málaga.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cerro-del-villar.jpg" alt="Cerro del Villar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miwipedia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cerro_del_Villar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
